{"G118":{"id":"G118","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0118","disambiguated_id":"G0118 =","unique_id":"G0118","headword":"ἀθλέω","transliteration":"athleō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to compete","definition_en":"ἀθλέω, -ῶ (in cl. also ἀθλεύω, ἆθλος, a contest, in war or in sport), \n to contend in games, wrestle, combat: 2Ti.2:5.†\n (AS)","source_line":215}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"regras","count":2}]},"G1567":{"id":"G1567","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1567","disambiguated_id":"G1567 =","unique_id":"G1567","headword":"ἐκζητέω","transliteration":"ekzēteō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to seek out","definition_en":"ἐκ-ζητέω, -ῶ \n [in LXX chiefly for דָּרַשׁ, also for נָצַר, בָּקַשׁ, etc. ;] \n__1. to seek out or after, search for: with accusative of person(s) (1Ma.9:26); figuratively, τ. κύριον, θεόν (cf. Psa.14:2, Amo.5:4, al.), Act.15:17, Rom.3:11, Heb.11:6; εὐλογίαν, Heb.12:17; ἐξεζήτησαν κ. ἐξηραύνησαν (as in 1Ma.9:26), sought and searched out: 1Pe.1:10. \n __2. As in 2Ki.4:11, Eze.3:18, 20 al. (דָּרַשׁ), to demand, require: Luk.11:50-51 †\n (AS)","source_line":1707}],"occurrence_count":7,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"requerido","count":2},{"gloss":"busque","count":2},{"gloss":"recompensador-que","count":1},{"gloss":"buscado","count":1},{"gloss":"inquiriram","count":1}]},"G1933":{"id":"G1933","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1933","disambiguated_id":"G1933 =","unique_id":"G1933","headword":"ἐπιεικής","transliteration":"epieikēs","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"gentle","definition_en":"ἐπιεικής, -ές\n (εἰκός, likely), [in LXX: Psa.86:5 (סַלָּח), Est.8:13 * ;] \n__1. seemly, fitting (Hom.). \n __2. equitable, fair, moderate: 1Ti.3:3, Tit.3:2, 1Pe.2:18, Jas.3:17; τὸ ἐ. (Thuc., i, 76), Php.4:5 (cf. Mayor, Ja, l.with, and see: ἐπιεικία).†\n ἐπιείκεια see: ἐπιεικία\n ἐπιεικία (Rec. -είκεια), -ας, ἡ \n (ἐπιεικής), [in LXX: Wis.2:19 12:18 Bar.2:27, from LXX Bar.4:24, TH (3:42), 2Ma.2:22 2Mac 10:4, 3Ma.3:15 3Mac 7:6 * ;] \nfairness, moderation, gentleness (\"sweet reasonableness,\" Matthew Arnold): Act.24:4; with πραΰτης, 2Co.10:1.†\n SYN.: πραΰτης (see Tr., Syn., § xliii) (AS)","source_line":2074}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"bondade","count":1},{"gloss":"sim","count":1},{"gloss":"sim-pacientes","count":1},{"gloss":"moderada","count":1},{"gloss":"brandos","count":1}]},"G2289":{"id":"G2289","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2289","disambiguated_id":"G2289 =","unique_id":"G2289","headword":"θανατόω","transliteration":"thanatoō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to kill","definition_en":"θανατόω, -ῶ \n [in LXX chiefly for מוּת hi., ho., also for הָרַג, etc. ;] \nto put to death: with accusative, Mat.10:21 26:59 27:1, Mrk.13:12 14:55, Luk.21:16, 2Co.6:9, 1Pe.3:18; pass., Rom.8:36. Metaphorical: Rom.8:13; pass., with dative, (in relation to), Rom.7:4.†\n (AS)","source_line":2438}],"occurrence_count":11,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"mortos","count":3},{"gloss":"matarão","count":2},{"gloss":"matarem","count":2},{"gloss":"matá","count":1},{"gloss":"vivereis","count":1},{"gloss":"somos-entregues-à-morte","count":1},{"gloss":"morto","count":1}]},"G2363":{"id":"G2363","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2363","disambiguated_id":"G2363 =","unique_id":"G2363","headword":"Θυάτειρα","transliteration":"Thuateira","lexical_morphology":"N:N--L","gloss_en":"Thyatira","definition_en":"Θυάτειρα, -ων, τά\n (-ας, ἡ, Rev.1:11 L; cf. WH, App., 156) \nThyatira, a city of Lydia: Act.16:14, Rev.1:11 2:18, 24.†\n (AS)","source_line":2512}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Tiatira","count":4}]},"G2489":{"id":"G2489","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2489","disambiguated_id":"G2489 =","unique_id":"G2489","headword":"Ἰωάννα, Ἰωανάν","transliteration":"Iōanna, Iōanan","lexical_morphology":"N:N-F-P","gloss_en":"Joanna","definition_en":"Ἰωάνα (TR, -ννα; se